
2025-10-03 Comments on productivity though not yet evidenced in a spec draft.

Glad to some activity, though evidence in the notes is scant. I see mention decision about "the" tech stack but ... not what it is. (I bet it is "a" tech stack and potentially will change...) But piloting fast to start getting on same page with customer is key. The first decisions are almost certainly not going to be the last, so don't get heavily invested in them. There will be many ways to think about and visualize these structures, we should not presume we find an effective way the first days in.

I think a tech stack as mentioned above implies infrastructure. What is it? Where is your code base? SVN? (I don't see it.) I hope we are not using resources outside the scope of the assignment and syllabus.

What is the rest of the research community using for this? Are we reinventing wheels? Or improving them?

Do we have pictures illustrating what it looks like when the client is winning value from the tool set? (Answer is "no" of course, since I do not see anything in the repo to this effect.) What driving examples can we create with the customer to focus this activity?

Potentially it is a good risk reduction step to have one or two team members crafting a template proposal so there is already progress once some specifics start to fall into place. Classic mistake is to think linearly, like this is a BS intro course. We need to learn to blend multiple threads of activity.

